WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.088
Two quiet failure modes,
time and licenses.

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:04.162
Time first.

3
00:00:04.162 --> 00:00:07.681
Enable NTP and set the external
servers at the Grid level

4
00:00:07.681 --> 00:00:11.425
before you configure the Grid
Master and members as clients.

5
00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:16.014
The Grid Master then serves time to the
members inside the encrypted tunnel,

6
00:00:16.014 --> 00:00:20.675
and if it goes offline, the candidate
and members sync to the external servers.

7
00:00:20.675 --> 00:00:23.093
The STIG requires the external servers at

8
00:00:23.093 --> 00:00:25.650
the Grid level and
recommends at least three.

9
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:29.198
A clock more than five minutes
off is stepped immediately;

10
00:00:29.198 --> 00:00:30.750
a smaller error is slewed.

11
00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.057
Time isn't cosmetic here:
Grid synchronization,

12
00:00:34.057 --> 00:00:38.213
Kerberos-signed updates, and
DHCP failover all depend on it.

13
00:00:38.213 --> 00:00:42.021
One gap to note for your control mapping:

14
00:00:42.021 --> 00:00:49.524
NIOS lists NTP authentication keys of MD5,
DES and SHA-1 only, with no SHA-2 option.

15
00:00:49.524 --> 00:00:50.550
Licenses.

16
00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:54.993
Member licenses bind to a hardware
ID, Grid-wide licenses bind to the

17
00:00:54.993 --> 00:00:59.675
Grid Master and replicate, and
subscriptions expire with the contract.

18
00:00:59.675 --> 00:01:01.850
The trap is the temporary license.

19
00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.744
It lasts sixty days and can't be
renewed, and when it expires,

20
00:01:05.744 --> 00:01:09.475
the member's services stop and
it's evicted from the Grid.

21
00:01:09.475 --> 00:01:12.163
So never let a production
member run on one.

22
00:01:12.163 --> 00:01:15.228
Install licenses on both
nodes of an HA pair,

23
00:01:15.228 --> 00:01:19.912
and expect the NIOS and some add-on
licenses to restart the product.

24
00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.737
If the Microsoft Management
license expires,

25
00:01:22.737 --> 00:01:25.637
synchronization to the
Windows servers stops.

26
00:01:25.637 --> 00:01:29.084
For VMware, get permanent
keys by submitting

27
00:01:29.084 --> 00:01:32.250
each VM's hardware ID,
and allow a day or two.

28
00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:40.379
Sources: Infoblox NIOS 9.1.x Configuring
NTP (Grid and member), NTP clock behavior,

29
00:01:40.379 --> 00:01:48.758
NTP authentication keys; License types,
Expiring licenses, Installing licenses;

30
00:01:48.758 --> 00:01:53.760
vNIOS for VMware obtaining
permanent licenses;

31
00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.940
DISA Infoblox NIOS 9.x
STIG V1R1, V-285309.
